// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 05-statements/inherent_method_call_unsupported_neg_01.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A return-position shared receiver call now lowers, but binding the call
// result in a local initializer (`let result = cell.get();`) is still outside
// the admitted receiver-call shape. The calling definition is rejected with
// the per-definition capability rejection ZOM4099, projected on the function
// definition, never as an internal compiler error.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
